  "result": "I withdrew the `NRS_484B_253_o2` record as a plan defect on span `s2`. The validator's second defect can't be fixed inside a node record, so the record stays withdrawn until the planner reconciles the segmentation.\n\n- **Why it's a plan defect:** this node's segmentation calls `s2` (\"within an intersection\") a condition, but the accepted sibling `NRS_484B_253_o1` calls the same words a trigger. A repair can't change the segmentation. Leaving `s2` out isn't allowed either, because it's the condition that the turning vehicle is within the intersection.\n- **The `s8` defect:** that came from my previous record listing \"having so yielded\" twice, and could have been avoided. The withdrawal tells the planner to map `s8` once, as the single compliance composition of `o1`.\n- **The coder's WITNESS_FAIL fix, passed to the planner:**\n  - Check that the turning vehicle \"so yielded\" (`o1` complied with) only from its latest entry into the intersection up to the observation before its turn begins. The turn's start is the latest rise of `drv.motion.turning_left` since that entry.\n  - The check must not reach the judged observation, the other vehicle's entry. At that point `o1` is always violated while the vehicle turns, which is why `forbid` and `blind` came out compliant instead of violated and `blind` instead of unknown.\n  - Keep `branch_2` compliant: the turn began while the other vehicle was 15 m from the intersection at 15 m/s, so the turning vehicle did not yield.\n\nThe withdrawal is in `/local-scratch2/sma407/smoke31-run/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/results/smoke31-1111-0039/iter-005/repair/NRS_484B_253_o2/record.jsonl`.",
